### Create order (happy path — uses local mock payment)
POST http://localhost:8088/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "cust-1001",
  "amount": 499.00,
  "currency": "INR"
}

### Get order by id (replace ORDER_ID)
GET http://localhost:8088/api/v1/orders/ORDER_ID

### List orders
GET http://localhost:8088/api/v1/orders

### Trip circuit: make mock payment always fail
POST http://localhost:8088/mock/payments/always-fail?enabled=true

### Create order while payment is down (expect FAILED + fallback message)
POST http://localhost:8088/api/v1/orders
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "customerId": "cust-1002",
  "amount": 100.00,
  "currency": "INR"
}

### Heal mock payment
POST http://localhost:8088/mock/payments/always-fail?enabled=false

### Fail only the next payment call
POST http://localhost:8088/mock/payments/fail-next
